PERSON {"id":23091,"section":"persons","title":"Jason Gibbs","status":"live","uri":"persons/jason-gibbs","featuredImage":["#27400 Jason gibbs edited"],"body":"Jason Gibbs was elected to the Santa Clarita City Council in November 2020 and took his seat that December; he was the city's mayor in 2023.[1][2]\n\nHe first stood in 2018 and came ninth of fifteen candidates with 10,008 votes. In 2020 he was elected second of nine, with 29,474.[2] He began a second term in December 2024, which runs to 2028; the archive does not yet hold the 2024 election for his seat, and the City lists him as a sitting member in 2026.[1][2]\n\nThe City's biography says he holds bachelor's and master's degrees in mechanical engineering from Cal Poly and works in the aerospace industry as senior principal engineer of West Coast operations for GP Strategies Corporation, on the ground support equipment for rocket launch programs including the Delta II, Delta IV and Atlas V. Before the council he served on the advisory board of the Boys and Girls Club and on the executive boards of the Valley Industry Association and the WiSH Foundation.[1]","footnotes":[{"col1":"1","col2":"City of Santa Clarita, \"Councilmember Jason Gibbs,\" https://santaclarita.gov/city-council/jason-gibbs/, read 1 October 2026: the City's own biography of a sitting member.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"1","note":"City of Santa Clarita, \"Councilmember Jason Gibbs,\" https://santaclarita.gov/city-council/jason-gibbs/, read 1 October 2026: the City's own biography of a sitting member.","source":"editorial-2026"},{"col1":"2","col2":"Archive records: the City Council elections of 2018 and 2020, with their returns, and the office holdings for each term.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"2","note":"Archive records: the City Council elections of 2018 and 2020, with their returns, and the office holdings for each term.","source":"editorial-2026"}],"editorNotes":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"heading":null,"note":null,"position":null}],"fullName":"Jason Gibbs","occupation":"City council member","roles":["#18327 City Council Member"],"historicalEra":["#171 Contemporary (2010–present)"],"recordProvenance":"council_winners_and_terms.php, 29 September 2026: elected to the Santa Clarita City Council; public facts only; build_council_profiles.php, 1 Oct 2026: profile from the City's biography and the archive's returns; portrait per Nathan Imhoff","bodyAuthorship":"editorial-2026","recordDates":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"col4":null,"col5":null,"printed":null,"iso":null,"granularity":null,"label":null,"confirmed":null,"col6":null,"rejected":null}]}
{"id":29082,"section":"officeHoldings","title":"Jason Gibbs — Mayor, The City of Santa Clarita","status":"live","uri":null,"holdingPerson":["#23091 Jason Gibbs"],"holdingOffice":["#18431 Mayor"],"holdingBody":["#394 The City of Santa Clarita"],"termStart":"2023","termStartEdtf":"2023","selectionMethod":"rotated","howEnded":"expired","startEvidence":"certified","footnotes":[{"col1":"1","col2":"City of Santa Clarita, \"Councilmember Jason Gibbs,\" https://santaclarita.gov/city-council/jason-gibbs/, read 1 October 2026, which gave his mayoralty as 2023; the same page read on 4 October 2026 leaves its \"Mayoral Terms\" line blank.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"1","note":"City of Santa Clarita, \"Councilmember Jason Gibbs,\" https://santaclarita.gov/city-council/jason-gibbs/, read 1 October 2026, which gave his mayoralty as 2023; the same page read on 4 October 2026 leaves its \"Mayoral Terms\" line blank.","source":"editorial-2026"},{"col1":"2","col2":"The City gives each mayoralty by a single year. The council chooses its mayor in December, and the City's pages are not consistent about whether that year is the one in which the mayor was chosen or the one served.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"2","note":"The City gives each mayoralty by a single year. The council chooses its mayor in December, and the City's pages are not consistent about whether that year is the one in which the mayor was chosen or the one served.","source":"editorial-2026"}],"editorNotes":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"heading":null,"note":null,"position":null}],"recordProvenance":"record_city_mayors_2026_10_04.php, 4 October 2026: from the City's council pages","recordDates":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"col4":null,"col5":null,"col6":null,"printed":null,"iso":null,"granularity":null,"label":null,"confirmed":null,"rejected":null}]}
{"id":27410,"section":"officeHoldings","title":"Jason Gibbs — City Council Member, The City of Santa Clarita","status":"live","uri":null,"holdingPerson":["#23091 Jason Gibbs"],"holdingOffice":["#18327 City Council Member"],"holdingBody":["#394 The City of Santa Clarita"],"holdingDistrict":["#25155 Santa Clarita City Council, District 3"],"termStart":"December 2024","termStartEdtf":"2024-12","termEnd":"December 2028","termEndEdtf":"2028-12","seatLabel":"District 3","selectionMethod":"appointed","howEnded":"serving","startEvidence":"certified","footnotes":[{"col1":"1","col2":"The term's end is derived. The City lists him as \"Councilmember Jason Gibbs, District 3\" (City of Santa Clarita, City Council, https://santaclarita.gov/city-council/, read 3 October 2026) and says that \"two district seats were voted upon in November 2024, so the remaining three district seats will be up for election starting in November 2026\" (City of Santa Clarita, District Elections, https://santaclarita.gov/districtelections, read 3 October 2026). His at-large term of 2020 ended in December 2024, so his District 3 seat was one of the two elected that November; four years from December 2024 is December 2028. The District 3 canvass is not yet in the archive.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"1","note":"The term's end is derived. The City lists him as \"Councilmember Jason Gibbs, District 3\" (City of Santa Clarita, City Council, https://santaclarita.gov/city-council/, read 3 October 2026) and says that \"two district seats were voted upon in November 2024, so the remaining three district seats will be up for election starting in November 2026\" (City of Santa Clarita, District Elections, https://santaclarita.gov/districtelections, read 3 October 2026). His at-large term of 2020 ended in December 2024, so his District 3 seat was one of the two elected that November; four years from December 2024 is December 2028. The District 3 canvass is not yet in the archive.","source":"editorial-2026"},{"col1":"2","col2":"County of Los Angeles Registrar-Recorder/County Clerk, final list of cancelled elections, November 5, 2024, https://content.lavote.gov/docs/rrcc/documents/cancelled-elections-november-2024.pdf: \"Santa Clarita (Council District 3)\" is listed under \"appointment in lieu of election due to insufficiency of candidates.\" He was the only candidate, so no vote was taken and he was appointed to the seat.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"2","note":"County of Los Angeles Registrar-Recorder/County Clerk, final list of cancelled elections, November 5, 2024, https://content.lavote.gov/docs/rrcc/documents/cancelled-elections-november-2024.pdf: \"Santa Clarita (Council District 3)\" is listed under \"appointment in lieu of election due to insufficiency of candidates.\" He was the only candidate, so no vote was taken and he was appointed to the seat.","source":"editorial-2026"}],"footnotesOn":["#25151 Final lists of cancelled elections: November 2020, 2022 and 2024"],"editorNotes":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"heading":null,"note":null,"position":null}],"recordProvenance":"fix_gibbs_current_term.php, 2 October 2026","recordDates":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"col4":null,"col5":null,"printed":null,"iso":null,"granularity":null,"label":null,"confirmed":null,"col6":null,"rejected":null}]}
{"id":23359,"section":"officeHoldings","title":"Jason Gibbs — City Council Member, The City of Santa Clarita","status":"live","uri":null,"holdingPerson":["#23091 Jason Gibbs"],"holdingOffice":["#18327 City Council Member"],"holdingBody":["#394 The City of Santa Clarita"],"termStart":"December 2020","termStartEdtf":"2020-12","termEnd":"December 2024","termEndEdtf":"2024-12","selectionMethod":"elected","howEnded":"reelected","startEvidence":"roster","endEvidence":"derived","footnotes":[{"col1":"1","col2":"Elected on November 3, 2020, second of 9 candidates for 2 seats, with 29,474 votes.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"1","note":"Elected on November 3, 2020, second of 9 candidates for 2 seats, with 29,474 votes.","source":"editorial-2026"},{"col1":"2","col2":"The term's end is derived: four years from its start. In 2024 the council began electing by district, and the District 3 canvass, which may name this seat, is not held. Terms turn over in December: Cameron Smyth left the council on 10 December 2024.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"2","note":"The term's end is derived: four years from its start. In 2024 the council began electing by district, and the District 3 canvass, which may name this seat, is not held. Terms turn over in December: Cameron Smyth left the council on 10 December 2024.","source":"editorial-2026"},{"col1":"3","col2":"No declaring document is held: the outcome rests on the count and on CEDA, the state's compilation of local results, which marks the same winner. California Elections Data Archive (CEDA), Center for California Studies and Institute for Social Research, California State University, Sacramento, with the Secretary of State: the 2020 candidates file (CEDA2020Data.xlsx), a compilation of the counties' returns, not a certified return.","col3":"editorial-2026","number":"3","note":"No declaring document is held: the outcome rests on the count and on CEDA, the state's compilation of local results, which marks the same winner. California Elections Data Archive (CEDA), Center for California Studies and Institute for Social Research, California State University, Sacramento, with the Secretary of State: the 2020 candidates file (CEDA2020Data.xlsx), a compilation of the counties' returns, not a certified return.","source":"editorial-2026"}],"editorNotes":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"heading":null,"note":null,"position":null}],"recordProvenance":"council_winners_and_terms.php, 29 September 2026","recordDates":[{"col1":null,"col2":null,"col3":null,"col4":null,"col5":null,"printed":null,"iso":null,"granularity":null,"label":null,"confirmed":null,"col6":null,"rejected":null}]}
